Apple may be exploring a way to let search providers show sponsored results inside <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/visual-intelligence/">Visual Intelligence</a>, according to code uncovered in <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-27/">iOS 27</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2025/06/ios-26-visual-intelligence-ask.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1008175" /><br/>
<br/>
The find comes from <em>MacRumors</em>' <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/author/aaron-perris/">Aaron Perris</a>, who said in a <a href="https://x.com/aaronp613/status/2097889181716385943">post on X</a> that the code points to Apple allowing search providers to insert their own sponsored results into &zwnj;Visual Intelligence&zwnj;, rather than Apple selling the ad space itself. He compared it to the sponsored product listings already seen on Amazon and Google. It is not clear whether Apple would take a cut of ad revenue.<br/>
<br/>
The feature would let third party search providers, such as Google, insert items such as sponsored product images alongside the organic results &zwnj;Visual Intelligence&zwnj; already returns when a user points their camera at an item to shop for it. That would set it apart from the advertising pushes Apple has driven directly in its own apps over the past year.<br/>
<br/>
Apple has been steadily expanding its advertising business across the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/app-store/">App Store</a> and Maps. The company began showing <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/01/23/more-app-store-ads-coming-soon/">additional sponsored slots</a> in &zwnj;App Store&zwnj; search results in March, and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/25/apple-maps-ads-live/">ads went live in Apple Maps</a> in the United States and Canada last month.<br/>
<br/>
